# Settings for THIS computer. Copy this file, then edit the copy:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored: your ports, IDs, camera addresses and account names stay on your machine and are never committed.
# Nothing here is required. The web app finds your arms and cameras by itself (run ./setup.sh, then open "Motor IDs").
# Everything below is commented out, so copying the file changes nothing until you remove a "#".
#
# Rules: one NAME=value per line; the real environment wins (FOLLOWER_ID=other uv run so101 start still works);
# $OTHER_NAME and ${OTHER_NAME} are expanded; "#" starts a comment. A .env is not read in demo mode.
# Where it is looked for: SO101_ENV_FILE, then the repo folder, then ~/.so101/.env. Run `uv run so101 env` to see which
# files were found and which names they set (never the values).
#
# Never put a password or API key anywhere else: keep it here, or log in with the tool's own login (huggingface-cli login).

# --- Names of the saved calibrations (the app and the scripts) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# FOLLOWER_ID=my_follower
# LEADER_ID=my_leader
# Where LeRobot keeps calibration files (default: ~/.cache/huggingface/lerobot/calibration)
# HF_LEROBOT_CALIBRATION=

# --- Cameras (the app) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Cameras page finds them for you. Use these to force a choice, for example on a Raspberry Pi with fixed USB sockets.
# A number (0, 1) or, on Linux, a device path such as /dev/v4l/by-path/... (it keeps pointing at the same USB socket when you re-plug).
# CAMERA_INDEX=0
# CAMERA2=
# Cameras served by another computer (for example a Raspberry Pi running `so101 start --camera-only`), comma separated:
# CAMERA_URL=http://<pi-address>:8000/raw.mjpg,http://<pi-address>:8000/raw2.mjpg

# --- Two computers (the app) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mirror the arms of another running copy of the app, for example the computer the arms are plugged into:
# SO101_REMOTE=http://<other-computer>:8000
# Where `so101 mcp` finds the running app (default http://127.0.0.1:8000):
# SO101_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Where your settings, roles and progress are stored (default ~/.so101):
# SO101_HOME=

# --- Command-line scripts in scripts/ (the web app does NOT need these) ---------------------------------------------------------
# macOS: /dev/tty.usbmodemXXXXXXXX   Linux / Raspberry Pi: /dev/ttyACM0   Windows: COM3
# FOLLOWER_PORT=/dev/ttyACM0
# LEADER_PORT=/dev/ttyACM1
# Hugging Face (only for recording and training with LeRobot)
# HF_USER=your-hf-username
# DATASET_REPO=${HF_USER}/so101_task
# TASK=Pick up the object
